WEBVTT

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:08.926
<v Hannah Brooks>Morning everyone! Hope you all managed to stay cool yesterday, that heat wave was no joke.</v>

00:00:10.659 --> 00:00:16.955
<v Jessica Tran>Morning! My AC barely kept up, but at least the dog was happy to nap all day.</v>

00:00:18.159 --> 00:00:25.196
<v Marcus Lee>Hey all. I actually went for a run at 6am to beat the heat, but it was still rough.</v>

00:00:26.207 --> 00:00:31.392
<v Samantha Ortiz>Good morning! I just stayed inside and caught up on Stranger Things. Highly recommend.</v>

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:36.310
<v Derek Patel>Morning! I think my plants are the only ones thriving right now.</v>

00:00:37.342 --> 00:00:45.120
<v Hannah Brooks>Alright, let’s get started. Two quick updates: First, the onboarding for the new dispatch coordinator is on track for next Monday.</v>

00:00:46.886 --> 00:00:56.146
<v Hannah Brooks>Second, we got the final numbers from the engagement survey—participation was 87%, which is up 6% from last quarter. Nice work on the reminders, everyone.</v>

00:00:57.166 --> 00:01:00.500
<v Jessica Tran>That’s awesome! I think the Slack nudges really helped.</v>

00:01:01.267 --> 00:01:06.453
<v Marcus Lee>Agreed, and the QR codes in the break room were a good call too.</v>

00:01:06.969 --> 00:01:14.006
<v Hannah Brooks>Thanks, team. Next up: we need to review the Remote Work Stipend Policy, specifically the section on ineligible expenses.</v>

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:27.282
<v Samantha Ortiz>Right now, it says any expenses not listed as eligible must be pre-approved by the HR Business Partner, which is Daniel Rios. Suspension for submitting ineligible expenses is up to 2 months.</v>

00:01:28.693 --> 00:01:36.100
<v Derek Patel>We’ve had a few cases where people were confused about who to contact, since Daniel moved to the compliance team.</v>

00:01:37.118 --> 00:01:43.414
<v Jessica Tran>Should we update the approver to Priya Desai? She’s been handling most of the HRBP duties lately.</v>

00:01:44.752 --> 00:01:52.160
<v Marcus Lee>Makes sense. Also, is 2 months suspension too harsh? We had that one case last quarter where it felt excessive.</v>

00:01:53.234 --> 00:01:59.160
<v Samantha Ortiz>I agree, maybe 1 month is more reasonable. It’s still a deterrent but not as punitive.</v>

00:01:59.768 --> 00:02:06.435
<v Derek Patel>I’m not sure about reducing the suspension. Won’t that make people more likely to try submitting ineligible stuff?</v>

00:02:08.163 --> 00:02:14.459
<v Jessica Tran>I get your point, Derek, but we haven’t seen repeat offenders. Most people just need clearer guidance.</v>

00:02:15.302 --> 00:02:20.857
<v Marcus Lee>Yeah, and Priya’s been good about communicating what’s allowed. I think 1 month is fair.</v>

00:02:22.192 --> 00:02:34.415
<v Hannah Brooks>Thanks for raising the concern, Derek. After reviewing the recent cases and feedback, we’re going to move forward with updating the approver to Priya Desai and reducing the suspension duration to 1 month.</v>

00:02:36.086 --> 00:02:42.752
<v Samantha Ortiz>I’ll take the action item to update the policy doc and notify the team in the next newsletter.</v>

00:02:44.190 --> 00:02:49.745
<v Derek Patel>Sounds good. Can you also flag it in the #people-ops Slack channel when it’s live?</v>

00:02:50.492 --> 00:02:55.307
<v Samantha Ortiz>Will do! I’ll aim to have it updated by end of day tomorrow.</v>

00:02:56.571 --> 00:03:01.757
<v Jessica Tran>Just to confirm, the rest of the ineligible expenses list stays the same, right?</v>

00:03:02.193 --> 00:03:05.527
<v Hannah Brooks>Correct, only the approver and suspension duration are changing.</v>

00:03:07.095 --> 00:03:08.595
<v Marcus Lee>Great, thanks for clarifying.</v>

00:03:09.672 --> 00:03:11.172
<v Jessica Tran>Thanks, Samantha!</v>

00:03:12.835 --> 00:03:14.335
<v Samantha Ortiz>No problem!</v>

00:03:15.168 --> 00:03:16.668
<v Derek Patel>Thanks everyone.</v>

00:03:17.302 --> 00:03:31.006
<v Hannah Brooks>Before we wrap up, one last thing: our contract with CleanFleet Janitorial is up for renewal next month. I’ll be reviewing their proposal this week, so let me know if you have any feedback on their service.</v>

00:03:32.118 --> 00:03:37.304
<v Marcus Lee>I’ll send you a note—there were a couple of missed trash pickups last month.</v>

00:03:38.358 --> 00:03:45.765
<v Jessica Tran>Overall they’ve been good, but I’d love to see if they can do a deeper clean in the kitchen area.</v>

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:49.612
<v Hannah Brooks>Noted, thanks. Anything else before we close?</v>

00:03:50.832 --> 00:03:52.332
<v Samantha Ortiz>All good here.</v>

00:03:53.815 --> 00:03:55.315
<v Derek Patel>Nothing from me.</v>

00:03:56.752 --> 00:04:00.456
<v Hannah Brooks>Alright, thanks everyone! Have a great rest of your week.</v>
